# Scripts keep the line endings their shell needs, whatever the clone's autocrlf says.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
# The vmangos patch is applied by git *inside a Linux container*, and the deploy project's
# Dockerfile is read there too: a CRLF checkout makes the patch fail to apply, which leaves the
# stock server (and no Skateboarding profession) behind.
*.patch    text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
